        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27011</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27011"/>
        <updated>2025-06-10T21:31:18.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">According to <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1965660#c8" rel="nofollow">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1965660#c8</a> <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/::-moz-focus-inner" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">::-moz-focus-inner</code></a> was effectively removed around FF89 (all this  issue does is final tidy up so that it is no longer in even parsed). The removal issue was <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1697053" rel="nofollow">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1697053</a></p>
<p dir="auto">What I've done is marked it as removed in FF89 and indicated this is deprecated rather than experimental.</p>
<p dir="auto">Is that OK, or should we note the final version FF140 ?</p>]]></content>
